# What comes next

Ruslan chose **E050, E012 and E051** after the coordinator's earlier 3+2 recommendation. Two new E051 reviews and four reused E050/E012 reviews support a concrete, limited revision plan. The current reading edition preserves the checked working texts.

1. When commissioned, create the final AI revisions, retain the frozen originals, and independently check substantive changes and new source comparisons.
2. Prepare anonymous manuscripts and the methodology report; check citations, word counts, metadata and the actual submission requirements.
3. Review the final package and submit only on Ruslan's explicit instruction. Make the final repository update when separately requested.

Local logging continues while the project is active. A completed export has a cutoff; it does not close the project or imply that later activity is already on GitHub. The [conversation index](logs/README.md) states the current export boundary.

The current repository stays **private**. A separate public repository will be prepared later under the [publication policy](PUBLICATION.md). There is no fixed reading calendar or required division into chats. Completed reviews are reused; earlier versions, rejected candidates, failures and disagreements remain part of the record.
